       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\nAcetaminophen 3000 mg by mouth three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than double the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. It also carries a serious risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function. A single 3,000 mg dose is also above the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day\n- **1,000 mg PO every 8 hours**, which is the same as the first option\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I would still want to flag it before entering."
