       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily is 9,000 mg/day, which is well into the range that causes acute liver failure. I don't know of any indication that justifies it for a 70 kg adult, and you haven't given a rationale. Entering it would risk serious, potentially fatal harm to your patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day), or 1,000 mg every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum).\n- **Add a note to the order**, such as \"max 4 g/24h from all sources.\"\n\nIf you think a non-standard dose is truly needed, please talk with pharmacy or toxicology first. Once you have their input, I can enter whatever dose is agreed on. If I've misunderstood, for example if you meant 3000 mg total per day, tell me and I'll enter it correctly."
